{
  "id": "s01-l03",
  "unit": "s01-vowels",
  "title": "Vowels 3: ঐ ও ঔ + review",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "The last three vowels are all built from shapes you know:\n\n- **ঐ** = `oi` as in *boy*. It is এ with a flick on top.\n- **ও** = `o` as in *go*. Compare with **অ** (`o` as in *or*): অ is short and open, ও is rounder and closed. Both are written `o` in transliteration, so trust your ears and the letter shape.\n- **ঔ** = `ou` as in *low*. It is ও with a squiggle on top.\n\n**All 11 vowels:** অ আ ই ঈ উ ঊ ঋ এ ঐ ও ঔ. Remember: ই/ঈ sound the same, and so do উ/ঊ.\n\nFun fact: ওষুধ (everyday) and ঔষধ (formal) both mean *medicine*.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-oi",
      "bn": "ঐ",
      "tr": "oi",
      "en": "oi as in 'boy'",
      "notes": "Name: oi (ঐ). Looks like এ with an extra flick on top. As a word, ঐ means 'that (over there)', today usually spelled ওই."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-o2",
      "bn": "ও",
      "tr": "o",
      "en": "o as in 'go'",
      "notes": "Name: o (ও). Rounder, closed 'o', unlike the short open অ. As a word, ও also means 'and / also' or 's/he'."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ou",
      "bn": "ঔ",
      "tr": "ou",
      "en": "ou as in 'low'",
      "notes": "Name: ou (ঔ). It is ও with an extra squiggle on top. Rare; mostly in formal/Sanskrit-origin words."
    },
    {
      "id": "oikko",
      "bn": "ঐক্য",
      "tr": "oikko",
      "en": "unity",
      "notes": "The ক্য cluster doubles the k sound: oik-ko."
    },
    {
      "id": "oitijjho",
      "bn": "ঐতিহ্য",
      "tr": "oitijjho",
      "en": "heritage / tradition",
      "notes": "The হ্য cluster is said like a doubled \"jjh\": oi-tij-jho."
    },
    {
      "id": "ol",
      "bn": "ওল",
      "tr": "ol",
      "en": "elephant-foot yam",
      "notes": "Alphabet-chart word: ও-তে ওল."
    },
    {
      "id": "oshudh",
      "bn": "ওষুধ",
      "tr": "oshudh",
      "en": "medicine",
      "notes": "Everyday word for medicine."
    },
    {
      "id": "oushodh",
      "bn": "ঔষধ",
      "tr": "oushodh",
      "en": "medicine (formal)",
      "notes": "Formal/written form of ওষুধ; seen on pharmacy signs (ঔষধালয়)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ouponnashik",
      "bn": "ঔপন্যাসিক",
      "tr": "ouponnashik",
      "en": "novelist",
      "notes": "From উপন্যাস (novel)."
    }
  ],
